---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Quant"
  description="Quantitative research projects: cross-sectional alpha research on WorldQuant BRAIN, Kalman-filtered high-frequency market microstructure, and a pre-registered equity momentum pipeline."
  bgImage="/bg/quant.jpeg"
>
  <div data-lang="en">
    <h1>Quantitative Trading</h1>
    <p>
      Side projects applying signal-processing and statistical methods from physics to
      financial markets. Interactive plots will land on individual project pages here as
      they're ready.
    </p>

    <div class="card-stack">
      <article class="project-card">
        <h3>Cross-Sectional Equity Momentum Pipeline</h3>
        <p class="role">
          Python &middot; S&amp;P 500 &middot; Apr 2026 &ndash; Present &middot;
          <a href="https://github.com/NoahZ969/momentum-pipeline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          An end-to-end quantitative research pipeline, validated by reproducing the
          well-documented 12&ndash;1 cross-sectional momentum anomaly (Jegadeesh &amp;
          Titman 1993; Asness, Moskowitz &amp; Pedersen 2013). Built around a
          pre-registered analysis plan: point-in-time S&amp;P 500 membership to
          eliminate survivorship bias, in-sample 2005&ndash;2019 with a frozen
          2020&ndash;2025 holdout, and pre-committed interpretation buckets for the
          resulting Sharpe. The goal is a measurement apparatus I can trust &mdash;
          once validated, the pipeline becomes the substrate for evaluating novel
          hypotheses with calibrated confidence.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="project-card">
        <h3>WorldQuant Int&rsquo;l Quant Championship 2026 &mdash; Stage 2, USA Region</h3>
        <p class="role">BRAIN &middot; Fast Expression DSL &middot; Mar 2026 &ndash; May 2026</p>
        <p>
          Submitted 11 cross-sectional alphas on the TOP3000 USA universe (delay-1,
          subindustry-neutral); the four best-performing held out-of-sample Sharpe
          1.3&ndash;2.0 across the full 2019&ndash;2023 window (best single alpha 1.98),
          with turnover 20&ndash;45%, max drawdown under 7%, and self-correlation below
          0.7. The useful result was methodological: ablating a fundamental-anchored
          composite (Sharpe 1.59) collapsed it to &minus;0.35 once the price-volume
          component was removed, showing the alpha had inherited the pool&rsquo;s PV
          signal rather than diversifying it &mdash; so every ingredient now gets a
          standalone-Sharpe check before any multi-field combination. Searching a fixed
          six-transform template across BRAIN&rsquo;s data sub-categories (100+ logged
          field &times; transform simulations) decouples field selection from formula
          design and turns alpha search into a measurable hit-rate problem. Advanced past
          Stage 1 among 156,000+ registrants.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="project-card">
        <h3>High-Frequency Market Microstructure Signal Extraction</h3>
        <p class="role">Python &middot; Kalman Filter &middot; MLE &middot; Aug 2025 &ndash; Feb 2026</p>
        <p>
          A Kalman filter that separates the efficient price signal from microstructure
          noise (bid-ask bounce) in high-frequency Bitcoin tick data, modeling price as
          a random walk with mean-reverting error. Process and measurement noise matrices
          (Q and R) are calibrated by MLE; anchoring measurement noise to empirical
          tick-size volatility resolves regime-switching overfitting. Benchmarked against
          the EM algorithm (<code>pykalman</code>), with superior signal retention in
          high-volatility regimes.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="empty">More projects in progress.</p>
  </div>

  <div data-lang="zh">
    <h1>量化交易</h1>
    <p>
      将物理学中的信号处理与统计方法应用于金融市场的业余项目。未来的交互式可视化
      将作为独立的项目子页面在此呈现。
    </p>

    <div class="card-stack">
      <article class="project-card">
        <h3>股票截面动量策略流水线</h3>
        <p class="role">
          Python &middot; S&amp;P 500 &middot; 2026 年 4 月 &ndash; 至今 &middot;
          <a href="https://github.com/NoahZ969/momentum-pipeline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          一套端到端的量化研究流水线，通过复现广泛验证过的 12&ndash;1 截面动量异象
          （Jegadeesh &amp; Titman 1993；Asness, Moskowitz &amp; Pedersen 2013）来验证其可靠性。
          整个项目围绕预注册（pre-registered）的分析方案构建：采用按时间点的 S&amp;P 500
          成分股以消除幸存者偏差；样本内为 2005&ndash;2019 年，2020&ndash;2025 年作为冻结的
          样本外检验区间；并预先约定夏普比率结果的解读区间。目标不是策略本身的盈利能力，
          而是建立一套可信赖的测量装置 &mdash; 一旦验证通过，这条流水线将成为之后评估
          新假设时具备校准置信度的基础设施。
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="project-card">
        <h3>WorldQuant 国际量化锦标赛 2026 &mdash; 第二阶段（美国赛区）</h3>
        <p class="role">BRAIN &middot; Fast Expression DSL &middot; 2026 年 3 月 &ndash; 2026 年 5 月</p>
        <p>
          在 TOP3000 美股股票池上提交了 11 个横截面 alpha（delay-1，子行业中性）；其中表现最佳的
          四个在 2019&ndash;2023 完整区间的样本外夏普比率达 1.3&ndash;2.0（单个最优为 1.98），
          换手率 20&ndash;45%，最大回撤低于 7%，自相关性低于 0.7。真正有价值的收获在方法论层面：
          对一个以基本面为核心的复合 alpha（夏普比率 1.59）做消融实验，剔除其量价分量后骤降至
          &minus;0.35，说明它只是继承了资产池原有的量价信号，而非提供了新的分散化来源 &mdash;
          此后任何多字段组合前，都会先行检验各成分的独立夏普比率。在 BRAIN 的各数据子类别上
          统一套用六种变换模板（累计记录 100+ 组字段 &times; 变换模拟），将字段选择与公式设计
          解耦，把 alpha 搜索转化为可量化的命中率问题。最终从 156,000+ 名参赛者中晋级第二阶段。
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="project-card">
        <h3>高频市场微观结构信号提取</h3>
        <p class="role">Python &middot; 卡尔曼滤波 &middot; 极大似然估计 &middot; 2025 年 8 月 &ndash; 2026 年 2 月</p>
        <p>
          针对高频比特币逐笔数据构建卡尔曼滤波器，将有效价格信号与微观结构噪声
          （买卖价差跳动）分离，把价格建模为带均值回复误差项的随机游走。通过极大似然估计
          （MLE）校准过程噪声与测量噪声矩阵（Q, R）；将测量噪声锚定于经验上的最小变动单位
          波动率，解决了状态切换带来的过拟合问题。与 EM 算法（<code>pykalman</code>）
          进行了对比测试，在高波动区间表现出更优的信号保留能力。
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="empty">更多项目进行中。</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
